This is the ClimateCalendar project for the Gemma 4 Good Hackathon (May 18, 2026 deadline).

Project goal:
Climate-adapted planting companion for smallholder farmers, powered by Gemma 4 E4B running offline. Gives farmers per-GPS, per-crop recommendations grounded in 30+ years of weather data, ENSO forecasts, soil profile, and live observations. Multilingual (140 languages via Gemma).

Architecture constraints:
- All code must work offline (no cloud LLM calls in production)
- Gemma 4 inference uses transformers AutoModelForMultimodalLM (NOT AutoModelForCausalLM — Gemma 4 is multimodal)
- Function-calling tools live under src/tools/, one file per tool, with a single public function per file
- Every tool returns a JSON-serializable dict or list
- Type hints on every function signature
- No banned-pesticide recommendations: filter against data/banned_pesticides_by_country.json
- Target user: smallholder farmer; tone is plain, language is the farmer's local language

Code style:
- Functions under 40 lines when possible
- Network calls always have timeout=30 and call raise_for_status()
- Use TypedDict or pydantic for return shapes when they're structured
- Add a __main__ block to each tool file with a quick smoke test

Free APIs we use (all keyless):
- Open-Meteo Historical + Climate (CMIP6 projections)
- NOAA ONI (CSV download for ENSO history)
- IRI ENSO Plume (ENSO forecast)
- ISRIC SoilGrids (REST)
- NASA POWER
- CHIRPS rainfall
- FAO ECOCROP (crop tolerance)
- Sentinel-2 NDVI via Google Earth Engine (free for research)

Local dev runs on Mac (CPU). Inference runs on Kaggle (T4 GPU). Final edge demo runs on Pi5 via Ollama (GGUF Q4_K_M).

When suggesting code, prefer keyless free APIs and never require credentials we haven't established.
